  "pivot": { "x": 48, "y": 48 },
  "registration": "center",
  "notes": [
    "Thirteen projectiles, each with three rows: flight (loops), impact (plays once and ends on an empty frame) and deflect (plays once, then flight carries on).",
    "Impact and deflect are alternatives chosen by the game when the projectile touches something. They are never played one after the other.",
    "There is no ground line. In flight and deflect the pivot (48, 48) is the weapon's centre, the flask's belly or the spell's core. In impact the pivot is the point of contact.",
    "'lead' is how far the first flight frame reaches ahead of the pivot. Add it along the direction of travel to find the tip when placing the impact.",
    "'impactAnchor' says where the impact is drawn: 'contact' at the point of the hit, 'recipient' on the body of whoever is healed, 'head' on the target's head. The last two can be played without any flight.",
    "'orient' is 'heading' for art drawn pointing along its travel, which is turned to the direction of flight, and 'fixed' for art that already tumbles in its frames, which is only mirrored.",
    "deflect F6 is the same picture as flight F1, so flight resumes at F2 ('next').",
    "'flightBounds' is the painted area of flight F1, trail included. It shows scale and is not a collision box.",
    "Speed, range, gravity, damage and collision size are gameplay values and live in the catalogs under data/."
  ],
